# 14. Cabinet Rules

The Cabinet is intended to contain proof of work.

## CP-CAB-001 — Every Applicable Module Has an Artifact
**Severity:** HARD

For module types that use Cabinet artifacts, `cabinetArtifact` metadata must exist.

## CP-CAB-002 — Artifact Has Name
**Severity:** HARD

Already covered by CP-FM-015.

## CP-CAB-003 — Artifact Has Description
**Severity:** HARD

Already covered by CP-FM-016.

## CP-CAB-004 — Artifact Has Unlock Condition
**Severity:** HARD

Already covered by CP-FM-017.

## CP-CAB-005 — Artifact Is Produced by the Work
**Severity:** HUMAN

The artifact must be something the learner produces by doing the module's work.

## CP-CAB-006 — Artifact Is Not Merely a Template
**Severity:** HUMAN

The Cabinet is not intended to be a collection of documents the learner simply downloads.

## CP-CAB-007 — Body/Metadata Consistency
**Severity:** WARNING / HUMAN

The artifact described in the body should correspond to the frontmatter artifact.

A deterministic check may compare obvious names, but should not require exact text matching.

