# 15. Access/Commercial Model Rules

CyberPivot is currently a paid platform with free Foundation content.

The current rule is:

- Foundation content is free/ungated.
- Role-path content is paid unless explicitly marked free.

## CP-ACCESS-001 — Foundation Access Classification
**Severity:** HARD only if access metadata exists in the implementation

Foundation content must not accidentally be classified as paid if the access-control implementation explicitly encodes its free status.

This rule must be implemented only after the actual access-control source of truth is confirmed.

## CP-ACCESS-002 — Role-Path Default Access
**Severity:** HARD only if access metadata exists

Role-path modules should follow the paid-by-default model unless explicitly marked free.

Do not implement this as a content-folder assumption if the actual application access logic is elsewhere.

## CP-ACCESS-003 — No Historical Open-Source Enforcement
**Severity:** HARD

Do not build QA rules based on the old open-source/freemium model.

Historical references to community contribution, open-source licensing, or free role-path content must not be treated as current content requirements.

